# Git push includes Vercel

When the user asks to **push to git** (including “please push to git”), that also means:

1. Commit if there are uncommitted changes they intend to ship (only when they asked to push / commit).
2. `git push` to the remote.
3. Deploy production with `npx vercel --prod --yes`.

Do not wait for a separate “and Vercel” request. Return the production URL when done (typically https://jsjobboard.vercel.app).
Deploy with the linked project under the **JS Valve's projects** team (`js-valves-projects/jsjobboard`), not Santa Fe Room / `jsjobboard-eight`.
